The error in your screenshot is:

Plain Text
Cannot find module 'node:path'

This usually means your Node.js version is too old for the version of React packages you installed.

Check Node version

Run:

Shell
node -v

and

Shell
npm -v
If Node is old (for example v12 or v14)

React packages may require a newer version.

Install a newer Node.js:

Shell
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_20.x | bash -
apt-get install -y nodejs

Then verify:

Shell
node -v
npm -v

Expected:

Plain Text
v20.x.x
Clean and reinstall packages

From your frontend folder:

Shell
rm -rf node_modules
rm -f package-lock.json

Install again:

Shell
npm install

Then:

Shell
npm start
Why this error happens

When React starts:

Plain Text
npm start
↓
react-scripts
↓
eslint
↓
eslint-config-react-app
↓
node:path

node:path is a built-in module available in newer Node.js versions.

If Node.js is old:

Plain Text
Cannot find module 'node:path'

appears and compilation fails.

Please run
Shell
node -v
npm -v

and paste the output. That will confirm whether the issue is an outdated Node.js version.

